      "claim_id": "CLM-0086-1",
      "note": "Reconstructed and re-derived end to end. (i) M=\u03c9^2\u2297W_5^\u2228 has deg M = 2(2g-2) - (4g+12-4f)|_{g=6,f=5} = 20-16 = 4 and h^0(L)=1+h^0(M) by \u03c7(L)=1 plus Serre duality; M is always special since h^1(M)=h^0(L)\u22651. (ii) h^0(L)=4 gives h^0(M)=3 = deg M/2 + 1, i.e. Clifford equality with deg M \u2209 {0,2g-2}, forcing C hyperelliptic and M\u2245(g^1_2)^{\u22972}. (iii) Castelnuovo\u2013Severi: a degree-2 and a degree-4 map to P^1 not factoring through a common map give g \u2264 (2-1)(4-1)=3 < 6; the common factor \u03c6 has deg \u03c6 | 2 and deg \u03c6 \u2265 2, so \u03c6 = h and \u03b3 = q\u2218h with deg q = 2. (iv) Splitting obstruction: h_*O_C = O\u2295O(-7) (branch degree 2g+2=14); q_*O(-7) = O(-4)^2 is forced for EVERY degree-2 q, since deg = -8 by \u03c7 and h^0(q_*O(-7)\u2297O(3)) = h^0(O(-1)) = 0 pushes the larger summand to \u2264 -4; hence E = O(1)\u2295O(4)^2, Sym^2E(-6) = O(-4)\u2295O(-1)^2\u2295O(2)^3 with h^0 = 9, and h^0(C,R\u2297\u03b3^*O(-6)) = 7 for R = O_{P(E^\u2228)}(2)|_C. Left-exactness gives h^0(F(-6)) \u2265 9-7 = 2, while balanced F = O(4)\u2295O(5) gives F(-6) = O(-2)\u2295O(-1) with h^0 = 0. The contradiction stands; every number was independently recomputed and agreed. The parenthetical 'does not require the weak relative-canonical normalization' is also true, but not for the reason written \u2014 see FC-0135-A.",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
    },
